Experimental source-kernel encrypted UEFI boot verification
Date: 2026-10-15
Target: QEMU/KVM qcow2 disk, serial GQ-TARGET-261014; no physical drives attached
Firmware: OVMF
Boot path: systemd-boot -> gentoo-experimental.efi -> Gentoo 7.2.10 initramfs

The first source UKI attempt stalled because the rehearsal target's installed
sys-apps/systemd-261.2 lacked its cryptsetup USE flag. Its persisted package.use
file also lacked that flag, despite config/packages.yaml and the repository
unit fixture specifying it. The corrected target package.use entry was
"sys-apps/systemd boot ukify cryptsetup". Portage source-built systemd-261.2;
the installed USE record now includes cryptsetup and
/usr/lib/systemd/systemd-cryptsetup exists.

Regeneration command:
  chroot /mnt/gentoo emerge --ask=n --config =sys-kernel/gentoo-kernel-7.2.10

The regenerated source UKI was inspected with lsinitrd. It contains the
systemd-cryptsetup binary, dracut-crypt-generator,
systemd-cryptsetup-generator, and dracut crypt module.

Boot observations:
  Gentoo Linux (2.18) (gentoo-experimental.efi) selected as default
  Linux version 7.2.10-gentoo-dist
  Command line included:
    rd.luks.name=ffd9a81f-d7a9-4efa-818f-7f6ab30dda28=gentoo-root
    root=/dev/mapper/gentoo-root rootflags=subvol=@ rw
  Initramfs found /dev/disk/by-uuid/ffd9a81f-d7a9-4efa-818f-7f6ab30dda28
  Cryptography Setup for gentoo-root completed after entering the temporary
  test passphrase; /dev/mapper/gentoo-root was found
  Btrfs mounted /, /home, /.snapshots, and /var/log from @, @home,
  @snapshots, and @log
  The guest reached the graphical target, started NetworkManager, sshd,
  SDDM, and the serial getty

SSH verification command (key-authenticated as rehearsal):
  uname -r
  systemctl is-system-running
  id
  findmnt -no SOURCE,FSTYPE,OPTIONS /
  findmnt -no SOURCE,FSTYPE,OPTIONS /home
  findmnt -no SOURCE,FSTYPE,OPTIONS /.snapshots
  findmnt -no SOURCE,FSTYPE,OPTIONS /var/log
  findmnt -no SOURCE,FSTYPE,OPTIONS /efi

Observed output:
  uid=1000(rehearsal) gid=1000(rehearsal) groups=1000(rehearsal),10(wheel)
  7.2.10-gentoo-dist
  running
  /dev/mapper/gentoo-root[/@] btrfs rw,noatime,compress=zstd:3,space_cache=v2,subvolid=256,subvol=/@
  /dev/mapper/gentoo-root[/@home] btrfs rw,noatime,compress=zstd:3,space_cache=v2,subvolid=257,subvol=/@home
  /dev/mapper/gentoo-root[/@snapshots] btrfs rw,noatime,compress=zstd:3,space_cache=v2,subvolid=258,subvol=/@snapshots
  /dev/mapper/gentoo-root[/@log] btrfs rw,noatime,compress=zstd:3,space_cache=v2,subvolid=259,subvol=/@log
  /dev/vda1 vfat rw,noatime,fmask=0077,dmask=0077,codepage=437,iocharset=ascii,shortname=mixed,errors=remount-ro

This validates the source experimental kernel's encrypted QEMU boot and
configured-user SSH login. It does not validate the physical GPU, network,
audio, suspend/resume, Secure Boot, or real firmware/device behavior.
